# superglue-kt JNI conventions

## JNI boundary

- Keep JNI methods thin — marshal JSON/strings across boundary; logic stays in Rust `native/`.
- Match error mapping documented in superglue-js types.

## Kotlin/Java module

- Public entry: `com.superglue.kt` package.
- Butler uses `com.butler.data.ai.SuperglueBridge` for safe probes when native lib absent.

## Rust native crate

- Build with NDK toolchain; do not assume host `cargo build` produces Android artifacts.
- After Rust API changes: rebuild JNI + reinstall on device/emulator.

## Testing without device

- JVM tests must pass when `.so` is missing (feature detection, not crash).
- Instrumented tests on emulator for full JNI path.

## Parity

Binding changes require cross-check with `superglue-js/index.d.ts` and py examples.
